# Architecture

Aether is a MERN TypeScript monorepo: `client/` (React + Vite), `server/` (Express), `shared/` (types/constants/schemas), MongoDB.

Layers: React → Express routes → controllers → services → models → MongoDB.
AI: Controller → AIProviderManager → provider adapter → external API.
Tools: AIProviderManager → ToolManager → tool implementation.

Never use Next.js, Firebase, or Supabase as the backend/database.
Never put business logic, provider SDKs, or database access in React.
Never call Gemini/OpenAI/etc. outside `server/src/services/ai/providers/`.
Application code talks to `AIProviderManager`, never to a vendor SDK.

Do not implement later phases while foundational errors remain.
Do not fake production AI, search, or storage. If a provider is missing, return a clear error. Mock AI only when `ENABLE_MOCK_AI=true`.
Do not make destructive git or file changes without checking existing code.
